ATP fixture for VMC-ATP-028. Test instrumentation, not part of the product.

Environment variables read by the patched example:
  ATP_EXECUTION=multi   ExecutionMode::MultiThreaded (unset: SingleThreaded)
  ATP_WORLD_DIR=<dir>   world directory (unset: world)
  ATP_TRACE_OUT=<path>  prefix of the output files (unset: atp-028)
It spawns 60 pigs in region (0,0) and 60 in region (-1,-1) from a fixed seed (gravity and
block collision on, every second pig walking) and records 120 ticks:
  <prefix>.trace        every pig's position, velocity and grounded flag per tick
  <prefix>.ticks        tick number and duration
  <prefix>.invocations  each per-region physics call: region, entities, thread, enter/exit ns
The server log gets "ATP trace complete, 120 ticks" when the files are written.
This patch also changes void/src/systems/physics.rs (temporary instrumentation).
Analyse the output with tools/atp/region-trace-analyze.py.

Apply at the repository root:   git apply tools/atp/patches/<this file>
Remove it after the test:       git apply -R tools/atp/patches/<this file>

